---
export const prerender = true;

import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const breadcrumbItems = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Privacy Policy', url: '/privacy' },
];

const pageTitle = 'Privacy Policy: Zero-Logging & Data Protection | myipv4v6.com';
const pageDescription = 'Comprehensive Privacy Policy for myipv4v6.com. Explaining our strict zero-logging architecture, in-memory edge processing, and complete absence of user tracking.';
---

<Layout
  title={pageTitle}
  description={pageDescription}
  canonicalUrl="https://myipv4v6.com/privacy"
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto w-full flex flex-col gap-8">
    <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbItems} />

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 border-b border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 pb-6">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-semibold text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z" />
        </svg>
        <span>Architectural Privacy Commitment</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-black tracking-tight text-neutral-950 dark:text-white">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-neutral-500">Effective Date: October 2026 • Document Version 2.0</p>
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-8 text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">1. Core Architectural Principle: Zero Logging</h2>
        <p>
          At <strong>myipv4v6.com</strong>, we believe privacy is not merely a policy statement—it is an architectural design constraint. The application itself does not log, store, track, or sell visitor IP addresses.
        </p>
        <p>
          When you connect to our service, your public IP address is transmitted in standard TCP/IP packet headers. This IP address is processed strictly in <strong>volatile RAM memory</strong> at the Cloudflare edge worker node nearest to you to render your response HTML or JSON. Upon completion of that HTTP transmission, your IP address is immediately discarded from memory.
        </p>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border border-emerald-200 dark:border-emerald-800 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-300 text-xs sm:text-sm">
          <strong>Key Guarantee:</strong> The application does not log, persist, archive, analyze, or write your personal IP address to any database, file system, disk storage, or search history repository.
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">2. No Tracking Cookies, Beacons, or Fingerprinting</h2>
        <p>
          We do not use:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-sm">
          <li>Tracking cookies, advertising identifiers, or session tokens.</li>
          <li>Cross-site tracking scripts, Google Analytics trackers, or Facebook/Meta pixels.</li>
          <li>Browser canvas fingerprinting, WebGL auditing, or device identification heuristics.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The only client-side storage we utilize is browser <code>localStorage</code> (e.g. your visual theme preference <code>theme = 'dark' | 'light'</code> and an optional private recent query cache). This data remains strictly in your personal browser and is never transmitted to our servers or third parties.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">3. How Search Queries & External Enrichment Work</h2>
        <p>
          When you use our IP lookup tool to query an IP address:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-sm">
          <li><strong>Server-Side Proxied Resolution:</strong> The enrichment query is executed by our edge server worker. The queried network or third-party database never sees your personal device's IP.</li>
          <li><strong>Third-Party Geolocation Providers:</strong> To provide accurate ISP and autonomous system (ASN) data, our edge server queries trusted geolocation databases (such as ipwho.is, IPinfo, or Cloudflare edge data). As part of normal HTTPS request routing, the queried target IP is transmitted securely to the provider's API.</li>
          <li><strong>24-Hour Public Data Caching:</strong> Public network intelligence (e.g., ASN, country, city, ISP name) for queried addresses is cached in Cloudflare Key-Value (KV) storage for 24 hours to maximize response speed and eliminate redundant API calls. <em>No association between the queried IP address and the person or device searching it is ever recorded or stored.</em></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">4. Cloudflare Global Edge Infrastructure</h2>
        <p>
          myipv4v6.com is deployed across Cloudflare's global edge network. Cloudflare operates as the underlying reverse proxy infrastructure to protect against Distributed Denial of Service (DDoS) attacks, terminate TLS/SSL cryptographic handshakes, and optimize edge packet routing. As with all internet infrastructure, Cloudflare handles IP packets at the network transport layer in accordance with strict global data privacy standards (including GDPR and SOC 2 Type II compliance).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">5. Abuse Prevention & Rate Limiting</h2>
        <p>
          To safeguard service availability from denial-of-service attempts and malicious scrapers, we implement short-lived rate-limiting counters. These counters are stored in ephemeral memory cache with an automatic 60-second expiration window and are continuously flushed.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">6. Compliance with International Privacy Laws (GDPR & CCPA)</h2>
        <p>
          Because we do not store, process, or sell personal identifiers or persistent browsing histories:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-sm">
          <li><strong>GDPR (European Union):</strong> We adhere to the Data Minimization principle (Article 5(1)(c)). No user tracking consent banner is required because no non-essential cookies or personal tracking data are collected.</li>
          <li><strong>CCPA / CPRA (California):</strong> We do not sell or share personal information under any circumstance.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-2 pt-2 border-t border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">7. Privacy Inquiries</h2>
        <p class="text-sm">
          For technical questions or audit inquiries regarding our zero-logging architecture, please contact our team at <code>privacy@myipv4v6.com</code>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
